{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-4-6","id":"msg_01N2xehZ59UJMF81wWXhtRAu","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"Two failures:\n\n1. **r2_2_extra_operand**: GNU gtsort quotes the operand with single quotes (`'cycle.txt'`) and adds a \"Try '...' --help\" line. Our implementation doesn't quote and doesn't have the help message. I need to fix the implementation.\n\n2. **r2_2_nonexistent_file**: GNU gtsort capitalizes \"No such file or directory\" while our implementation uses lowercase \"no such file or directory\". This is because `unwrapPathErr` returns the Go error string which uses lowercase.\n\nI need to fix `main.go` for both issues.\n\n\nFor the extra operand error, I need to match GNU's format by quoting the operand and appending a help message that references the program name from `os.Args[0]`, though I should verify how the reference test handles the full path variation.\n\nLooking at the normalization logic, the regex only catches lines starting with `tsort:`, so the \"Try\" line with the binary path won't be normalized. I need to add a normalizer that handles the help message line, either by stripping it or normalizing the path references so both outputs can be compared properly. The issue is that our binary would output a different path in the \"Try\" line each time since it's based on the test binary's location, so I need to normalize that away. Let me check how other commands in this repo handle similar extra operand errors to see if there's an established pattern.","signature":""}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":1,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1320,"cache_read_input_tokens":28119,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1320},"output_tokens":8,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"fa92a329-cbfc-4647-be2c-